recordStaticPath (:119-128) and forgetStaticPath (:130-138) share staticRelativePath (:591-598). It returns null for paths outside getLaravelStaticDir, for traversal (normalizeStaticPath) and for app_qy_v1/audio/, the same exclusion that staticFileEntries (:522-530) applies on rebuild. getStaticPath() resolves to the same root: config/storage.php:7 sets $staticPath = getLaravelStaticDir() on both OSes, so the vocabulary covers dir is in the kind. Each store is recorded only after it succeeds:
- CoverImageService: main cover :127 and thumbnail :154;
- VocabularyCoverService: the rename (:66-69) records only when File::move succeeds; regenerateWithAi records the cache file :293 and the cover :298, which covers both the cache-copy and the fresh branch;
- AssistMediaOperations submitCover :193;
- PostMediaController: images :128 and video :206;
- WordTranslationWriteback :690;
- ImageFileProcessor :315.
The delete paths CoverImageService::deleteCover :328 and VocabularyCoverService::deleteCoverFile :176 already forget. The grep of AppQyV1 for put/copy/move/unlink/delete/imagepng finds no other static-dir writer. The rest write under app_qy_v1/audio (their own kinds), the data dir or temp. The EdgeTTS hook in SentenceEnrichmentService :328 runs after the copy succeeds or the destination already exists. LearningController:268 is recorded as a known risk in the report, which the item allows. The re-run showed that without phpredis (available=false, backend database) every record/forget call is a no-op and raises no error.

